# Graphify-specific exclusions (OMS Task 9B.1 follow-up — Graphify hygiene).
#
# Merged with .gitignore by graphify (outer .gitignore rules first, this
# file last — gitignore last-match-wins semantics), so entries here can only
# ever exclude MORE than .gitignore already does, never re-include anything.
# This file exists because .gitignore's own scope is git-tracking, not graph
# indexing — several of these paths (e.g. storage/app/public uploads) are
# runtime-generated and were never meant to be walked by the AST extractor,
# but .gitignore alone did not stop that (see docs/DECISIONS_LOG.md,
# 2026-07-28 "Graphify hygiene" entry).
#
# Never index runtime/private/uploaded/cached/backup/secret-bearing content:
# uploaded financial attachments (payment/receipt proof images), compiled
# Blade view cache, session/queue-cache files, local backup archives, and
# the storage-linked encryption key file all live under storage/.
storage/**
bootstrap/cache/**
public/storage/**

# Third-party dependency source — never project-authored code to graph.
vendor/**
node_modules/**

# VCS internals and graphify's own output (also hardcoded by graphify itself,
# listed here for explicitness).
.git/**
graphify-out/**

# Secrets / environment configuration.
.env
.env.*

# Local SQL dumps/backups anywhere in the tree (none are git-tracked today —
# see the Task 9B.1 follow-up audit — but this stays fail-closed against a
# future one landing inside the repo by accident).
*.sql
